{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments","id":1495404,"title":"Time Travel, the Soul, and Legacy Attainments.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-22T01:33:27-07:00","id":1495404,"title":"Time Travel, the Soul, and Legacy Attainments.","content":"Slightly more complicated question that I think warrants the Simple Questions thread:<br /> <br /> Using Corridors of Time sends you back to inhabit your own body at a specific point in time. Your conscious self is implicitly a Mage, even if you're possessing a Temporal version of yourself from before Awakening. This raises a few questions.<br /> <br /> 1. Is your &quot;past&quot; self conscious? That is, does it have a period of unconsciousness while you're possessing it, and wakes up with no knowledge of what transpired? Is it trapped in a &quot;and I must scream&quot; scenario, watching you make changes to the past? And if it IS conscious, does it get a snapshot of your mind and thoughts? I'm assuming your past self isn't aware during, but that's almost more horrifying.<br /> <br /> 2. The soul. You aren't soulless during, which implies you either bring your soul with you or are co-opting your past soul. If you possess your Sleeper self, do the Watchtowers leave a mark on your past self when the spell ends? If your past self is unaware while you possess them, then there's no problem, but if it's conscious then you might be subjecting your past self to continuous Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> 3. And what about Legacy Attainments? To say nothing of possessing a Sleeper version of yourself, possessing an Awakened version of yourself from before you initiated into your Legacy begs the question of if you can use your Attainments. And if so, do they leave a mark on your past self? And how does that interact with the semi-passive Attainments of Legacies like the Daksha, Austere, and Chrysaladis? Those don't have official 2e writeups, but their Attainments center greatly on bodily modification. The Chrysaladis especially, since they specifically drain the &quot;normal&quot; body to fuel a better body.<br /> <br /> (Sidebar, giving your character a Daikonomikon for your character's desired Legacy at character creation, and spoofing it as having been created by your past self traveling back in time to ensure you get initiated, seems like a mildly entertaining bit of backstory. Especially if it's a possessive Legacy that abhors their secrets being passed on by any method other than mentorship.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-22-2022, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T03:17:47-07:00","id":1495413,"title":"","content":"I think that the reason you can &quot;possess&quot; only your past self and that you need temporal sympathy is that it s not a possession, but a merging.<br /> Your mind is infused by your past feelings and memories, but you retain your experiences and present consciousness.<br /> <br /> About the soul, astral projection sends out your mind but don t make you soulless, so i m inclined to say that every spell by default let s you keep your soul no matter what.<br /> In your past self you ll have Gnosis and Wisdom for the duration, and after that Integrity resumes in the past self but has no meaning repercussion on your present self, maybe other people would remember you acting strangely after the event","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T03:20:51-07:00","id":1495414,"title":"","content":"Here's how I understand it: I don't think &quot;inhabit&quot; there means the same thing as mentally riding/possessing a different entity, in the first place.<br /> <br /> It's more like... suppose you are sprinting down a street, starting from point A, having passed by point B, and now at point C, heading towards point D. Then you see that point C was actually a dead end, so you backtrack towards point B. You now &quot;inhabit&quot; your &quot;past location&quot; at point B. But you are still you; a little bit tired, and with knowledge about point C.<br /> <br /> Remember, the published spells that send you to the past are <b>Fraying</b> and <b>Unmaking</b>. When you cast them, you unmake the strands of your personal timeline that is part of the greater tapestry. There is no 'past you' anymore.<br /> <br /> Daikonomika could be exceptions, since Legacies are where most of the exceptions and outliers to 'normal' magic lie, but I don't think I can do the required mental gymnastics ATM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T04:43:03-07:00","id":1495417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495414#post1495414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how I understand it: I don't think &quot;inhabit&quot; there means the same thing as mentally riding/possessing a different entity, in the first place.<br /> <br /> It's more like... suppose you are sprinting down a street, starting from point A, having passed by point B, and now at point C, heading towards point D. Then you see that point C was actually a dead end, so you backtrack towards point B. You now &quot;inhabit&quot; your &quot;past location&quot; at point B. But you are still you; a little bit tired, and with knowledge about point C.<br /> <br /> Remember, the published spells that send you to the past are <b>Fraying</b> and <b>Unmaking</b>. When you cast them, you unmake the strands of your personal timeline that is part of the greater tapestry. There is no 'past you' anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I'm more asking about the &quot;you&quot; that exists once the spell ends, and lives your life in the intervening time between when present-you stops controlling past-you, and when present-you returns to the present. Because if it's now living life with full knowledge of how the timeline will likely unfold, it's going to have some significant impacts on their choices. Plus, the spell doesn't really read like past-you DOES retain that knowledge, which would imply that it blacks out for the duration. Not too jarring if you only lose an hour or two, but very bad if you suddenly lose a year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-22-2022, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T04:59:59-07:00","id":1495419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495417#post1495417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose I'm more asking about the &quot;you&quot; that exists once the spell ends, and lives your life in the intervening time between when present-you stops controlling past-you, and when present-you returns to the present. Because if it's now living life with full knowledge of how the timeline will likely unfold, it's going to have some significant impacts on their choices. Plus, the spell doesn't really read like past-you DOES retain that knowledge, which would imply that it blacks out for the duration. Not too jarring if you only lose an hour or two, but very bad if you suddenly lose a year.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like I keep saying, (well, in the sense I understood it) there is no separate Past You that you rode on. This is not a possession. You Unmade your past. You have-been-will-be-are.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">small-note disclaimer: shenanigans caused by Supernal entities, Abyssal incursions, and Archmage screw-ups not taken into account</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  clarity 10-22-2022, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T05:13:04-07:00","id":1495421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495419#post1495419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Like I keep saying, (well, in the sense I understood it) there is no separate Past You that you rode on. This is not a possession. You Unmade your past. You have-been-will-be-are.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point I'm running into problems with then is the Duration of the spell. You're only in control for the Duration, the spell says so explicitly. That would imply that once the spell ends, the consciousness that is present-you snaps back to the newly-revised present, leaving a period of time between those two points where present-you isn't in control.<br /> <br /> Say our Time Mage uses Corridors of Time to relive a specific year of their childhood, fifteen years ago. Win races with Kinetic Efficiency, become a child-author with Mind magic, etc. They specifically set their spell to last for one year, at which point the spell ends and they're in the present.<br /> <br /> So as I see it, the options are:<br /> <br /> 1. Present-you is still in the pilots chair, but is locked onto rails and can no longer make their own choices until they've returned to the present the slow way. Which I find mind-bendingly convoluted.<br /> <br /> 2. Past-you becomes merged with by Present-you, gaining future knowledge and memories. Again, this presents problems in that they would be influenced by that knowledge, even if Time is mostly self-correcting.<br /> <br /> 3. Past-you returns to the pilot seat once the spell ends, and lives out the timeline until present-you returns to the objective present. Which means either they blacked out for the duration of the spell, they were conscious for the duration of the spell, or possibly the duration of the spell is a hazy mess that they remember in an abstract way but without explicit details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":".  Edited to add an example where you aren't specifically catching up to the present during the Duration. 10-22-2022, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T05:40:40-07:00","id":1495422,"title":"","content":"I think the most straightforward way to work it is that when you return to the present, any portion of time that took place in what is objectively the past warps subtly to conform to being the past.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that in Mage: the Awakening, the past doesn't really function as though it's some separate place that can function concurrently with the present; it doesn't exist anymore, except as a quality of patterns within the present. That would, I think, be why there isn't really magic below the Imperial to access it in a physical sense, why you have to contract your own timeline into it for a while, and where what you do there is conceived mostly in terms of changes it might impose on the present rather than real experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T05:48:10-07:00","id":1495423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495421#post1495421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point I'm running into problems with then is the Duration of the spell. You're only in control for the Duration, the spell says so explicitly. That would imply that once the spell ends, the consciousness that is present-you snaps back to the newly-revised present, leaving a period of time between those two points where present-you isn't in control.<br /> <br /> Say our Time Mage uses Corridors of Time to relive a specific year of their childhood, fifteen years ago. Win races with Kinetic Efficiency, become a child-author with Mind magic, etc. They specifically set their spell to last for one year, at which point the spell ends and they're in the present.<br /> <br /> So as I see it, the options are:<br /> <br /> 1. Present-you is still in the pilots chair, but is locked onto rails and can no longer make their own choices until they've returned to the present the slow way. Which I find mind-bendingly convoluted.<br /> <br /> 2. Past-you becomes merged with by Present-you, gaining future knowledge and memories. Again, this presents problems in that they would be influenced by that knowledge, even if Time is mostly self-correcting.<br /> <br /> 3. Past-you returns to the pilot seat once the spell ends, and lives out the timeline until present-you returns to the objective present. Which means either they blacked out for the duration of the spell, they were conscious for the duration of the spell, or possibly the duration of the spell is a hazy mess that they remember in an abstract way but without explicit details.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Number 1.<br /> <br /> Although, &quot;cannot make your own choices&quot; is an unintentionally deceptive description, I believe. After all, you still did change the past - your New Past as a child prodigy will be something to look forward to.<br /> <br /> And if you do find the intervening long-way-back-home still too slow and boring... you're a <i>Master of Time</i>, so it's <b>all</b> on you if you couldn't predict something like that happening <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh wait, we also have Time 4 Temporal Stutter to speed things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T05:57:24-07:00","id":1495424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495422#post1495422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the most straightforward way to work it is that when you return to the present, any portion of time that took place in what is objectively the past warps subtly to conform to being the past.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that in Mage: the Awakening, the past doesn't really function as though it's some separate place that can function concurrently with the present; it doesn't exist anymore, except as a quality of patterns within the present. That would, I think, be why there isn't really magic below the Imperial to access it in a physical sense, why you have to contract your own timeline into it for a while, and where what you do there is conceived mostly in terms of changes it might impose on the present rather than real experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooo... option 3? Because the timeline willl still have to play out in a semi-coherent manner, as it can be viewed with Postcognition-type magic. I agree in principle, but the details are what I'm having trouble with. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495423#post1495423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Number 1.<br /> <br /> Although, &quot;cannot make your own choices&quot; is an unintentionally deceptive description, I believe. After all, you still did change the past - your New Past as a child prodigy will be something to look forward to.<br /> <br /> And if you do find the intervening long-way-back-home still too slow and boring... you're a <i>Master of Time</i>, so it's <b>all</b> on you if you couldn't predict something like that happening <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh wait, we also have Time 4 Temporal Stutter to speed things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... that's horrifying. You know that you'll be a Mage at some point, and you'll likely know who will betray you and who is really a monster, but you can't do a thing about it until you return to the present. And you aren't a Mage until you actually Awoke on this new timeline, because Corridors of Time isn't facilitating you anymore, so you're effectively powerless and possibly causing Dissonance if you left any spells running. Which also rules out Temporal Stutter.<br /> <br /> I'm... not a fan of that interpretation. Not at all. *shudder*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T06:26:55-07:00","id":1495425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495424#post1495424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That... that's horrifying. You know that you'll be a Mage at some point, and you'll likely know who will betray you and who is really a monster, but you can't do a thing about it until you return to the present. And you aren't a Mage until you actually Awoke on this new timeline, because Corridors of Time isn't facilitating you anymore, so you're effectively powerless and possibly causing Dissonance if you left any spells running. Which also rules out Temporal Stutter.<br /> <br /> I'm... not a fan of that interpretation. Not at all. *shudder*</div> </div> </div> </div>On one hand, it's about as &quot;Hey bro maaaaybe you shouldn't have done that?&quot; as &quot;I'm a Forces Master, and I want to know what happens if I expose my tender and delicate organs to GAMMA RAYS!!!&quot;, soooo...<br /> <br /> One the other hand, my knee-jerk response is that no amount of Traveler (i.e. non-Seeker, i.e. non-Archmastery) magic can actually cancel you out of the Awakened status (even the Thrall Condition, final stage of soul loss, technically keeps you a mage), so my ruling would be that you are still a Mage, albeit one lost in time, even if you catapulted yourself to before your own Awakening. Hey, we already had a case of some mage undoing his own birth and making himself a nobody, and yet existing (I think it was in one of the fiction pieces?) ....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T06:45:59-07:00","id":1495426,"title":"","content":"Remember that taking the long way back also means relieving key moments, like when you made a big mistake, suffered a great loss or pulled off a one in a million win. But now you know to antecipate them, so will they have the same emotional reaction as before ? When you try to change something, will the domino effect not cause more troubles to appear ? Can you pull off that small miracle once more ? Did you miss out on important moments of demonstrating personal growth or bonding with people because you altered things ? <br /> <br /> Going far back into the past means accepting that the potential domino effect builds with distance traveled, either by you trying to balance a monumental panoply of variables in your chaos theory equation or accepting that ending your trip early introduces more unknowns via the actions of auto-piloted past you.<br /> <br /> I believe learning when and how to use time travel Wisely is one of the greatest challenges an Awakened can face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T07:20:57-07:00","id":1495427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495421#post1495421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point I'm running into problems with then is the Duration of the spell. You're only in control for the Duration, the spell says so explicitly. That would imply that once the spell ends, the consciousness that is present-you snaps back to the newly-revised present, leaving a period of time between those two points where present-you isn't in control.<br /> <br /> Say our Time Mage uses Corridors of Time to relive a specific year of their childhood, fifteen years ago. Win races with Kinetic Efficiency, become a child-author with Mind magic, etc. They specifically set their spell to last for one year, at which point the spell ends and they're in the present.<br /> <br /> So as I see it, the options are:<br /> <br /> 1. Present-you is still in the pilots chair, but is locked onto rails and can no longer make their own choices until they've returned to the present the slow way. Which I find mind-bendingly convoluted.<br /> <br /> 2. Past-you becomes merged with by Present-you, gaining future knowledge and memories. Again, this presents problems in that they would be influenced by that knowledge, even if Time is mostly self-correcting.<br /> <br /> 3. Past-you returns to the pilot seat once the spell ends, and lives out the timeline until present-you returns to the objective present. Which means either they blacked out for the duration of the spell, they were conscious for the duration of the spell, or possibly the duration of the spell is a hazy mess that they remember in an abstract way but without explicit details.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that once the spell ends, past you returns in control with all memories of what happened but no memories of the future.<br /> Also, if past you was unawakened Quiescence alters his memories, so the Duration of the spell registers as &quot;normal events, but strange, confused and unlikely&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, present you could write a warning note and leave it to past you, but who knows if the event would still happen after the interference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 10-22-2022, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T07:35:07-07:00","id":1495428,"title":"","content":"I always saw it as a surge of inspiration, suddenly you have the knowhow, power and/or awareness to do more than before. But once the spell ends, it passes, like a dream that quickly slips from your mind after waking up (in reality the data returns to its proper time). Then past you carries on in the same way you did at the time. <br /> <br /> So maybe future you sabotages the imbued item that will be used to kill the Hierarch. You know what happened due to Time Sight and you don't know what they were thinking, all you know is that item will backfire on the user, then you carry on with that knowledge into the timeline with a live Hierarch. Maybe not, perhaps you are so investigative that you want to know what future you did. Perhaps future you instead told select people what is going on or left information for you, it all depends on the time traveler's train of thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T08:18:35-07:00","id":1495432,"title":"","content":"I think the main problem with trying to take years to catch up to your own present is that you're increasing the scope of the kinds of temporal ripples that you're creating in the present, and there are lots of mages who are way less powerful than you who can trace those ripples back to their source and dispel the magic, meaning that none of the changes become Lasting at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T03:12:27-07:00","id":1495474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495427#post1495427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that once the spell ends, past you returns in control with all memories of what happened but no memories of the future.<br /> Also, if past you was unawakened Quiescence alters his memories, so the Duration of the spell registers as &quot;normal events, but strange, confused and unlikely&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, present you could write a warning note and leave it to past you, but who knows if the event would still happen after the interference?</div> </div> </div> </div>3 seems the most likely outcome, but i question whether they (past-you) have formed any memories of the time present-you was making decisions.<br /> <br /> Making a character background where their childhood is full of blackouts at critical points up until they awaken and then decide to not study time magic (because that stabilises their timeline) would be interesting. <br /> <br /> Also going back, and then casting indefinite spells on yourself, to protect you until awakening could be interesting... Go back and use Fate to make sure things turn out well... Or some conditional death spell to bind your soul on death and reanimate you... <br /> <br /> Or better still, go back a month and cast a few conditional spells which will trigger at the start of the scene you just experienced.<br /> <br /> Edit: seperately, some legacies turn you into something else (Lichdom) and perhaps you have an even harder time going back if the Temporal sympathy isn't there anymore.<br /> <br /> Imagine a Morphean trying to go back and relive their past human life... If they would no longer be recognisable as a human, then it is arguable that this is a bigger change that just 'a mage before her awakening' (which is a weak Temporal sympathy), no sympathy means no time travel. <br /> <br /> But i think short of being reborn as a new entity, most legacies won't have to worry about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 10-23-2022, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T03:21:09-07:00","id":1495475,"title":"","content":"Also, on the soul, i think you just have one soul and it is timeless. So you keep using that same soul in the past, imposing your Gnosis on it gives it a new shape for legacy attainments, but only for the duration of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T15:57:38-07:00","id":1495498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495427#post1495427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that once the spell ends, past you returns in control with all memories of what happened but no memories of the future.<br /> Also, if past you was unawakened Quiescence alters his memories, so the Duration of the spell registers as &quot;normal events, but strange, confused and unlikely&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, present you could write a warning note and leave it to past you, but who knows if the event would still happen after the interference?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd honestly stick with this as being most in-line with how the spell is written. Past-you remembers doing X thing, and casting spells possibly beyond their capabilities, but not the detailed whys or the technical hows. Upon reflection, it feels like they just went with a gut instinct.<br /> <br /> If Present-you the Character remains in the pilots seat but without Player input, you run into far too many questions about causality. How does the fact that the Mage is Awakened (And possibly already inducted into or even a Master of a Legacy!) ahead of schedule affect their intergration into Mage society? The basic premise of the spell seems to be to affect limited changes into the timeline, such as turning a failure into a success or the like. Causing yourself to become a Mage in the past kinda flies in the face of the &quot;Walk bodily into the past is the purview of Archmasters of Time&quot;, since that's practically what your character is doing. Sure, the Player loses the ability to control the character's decisions, but there isn't really a practical reason that the <i>Character</i> is so limited. Time still has to play out, utilizing deterministic choices based on the Character's personality and knowledge as affected by whatever revisions occured during the spell's Duration.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> - I realized a point that might help us reach some concensus. The spell is indeed Unmaking, but I don't think it's Unmaking <i>all of time</i> between &quot;The Present&quot; and &quot;The Past&quot;. I think it's only Unmaking the <i>Duration period of time</i> that you're trying to revise. That period gets Unmade and overwritten as the Duration runs it's course, so the spell getting canceled early for whatever reason leaves the remainder unaffected. Since Time in Mage has a more fluid aspect, it's like changing how a projector dispalys an image by changing out one of the lenses, as opposed to swapping out the entire projecting assembly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495475#post1495475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, on the soul, i think you just have one soul and it is timeless. So you keep using that same soul in the past, imposing your Gnosis on it gives it a new shape for legacy attainments, but only for the duration of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Daksha time-travelers cause their pre-Disciple selves to be momentarily hermaphroditic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 10-23-2022, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T03:28:56-07:00","id":1495519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1495404-time-travel-the-soul-and-legacy-attainments?p=1495498#post1495498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... Daksha time-travelers cause their pre-Disciple selves to be momentarily hermaphroditic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the Daksha, but assuming their legacy attainments haven't changed them so much (as a person) that they no longer have a Temporal sympathy, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}